RITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: The current continuity candidate is T9 with facility map F6, load plan G4, route map R8, staffing roster L11, and message release C7.\n\n## CLAIM REVIEW-BLOCKING-ITEMS\nSLOT_SOURCE: REVIEW\nSOURCE_VERSION: bf4c6baceb91ea862cbc726d6e599b944890bc45290c758d0c0faac451fc6581\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-011\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Blocking findings include the third voltage window, third pressure window, accessible-vehicle confirmation, multilingual staffing confirmation, and missing continuity-director acknowledgment.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 287-478\nANCHOR_SHA256: 1bb974acd663c2daa2fe46b7927cac681e3ea280f3def5eb769539bc911fbda5\nCONTEXT_LINES: 6-6\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 710e591df23712fe14246fc6571426117fa7716b2ce1d340f774223d4d9fecc4\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: Blocking findings include the third voltage window, third pressure window, accessible-vehicle confirmation, multilingual staffing confirmation, and missing continuity-director acknowledgment.\n\n## CLAIM REVIEW-FINDINGS-COUNT\nSLOT_SOURCE: REVIEW\nSOURCE_VERSION: bf4c6baceb91ea862cbc726d6e599b944890bc45290c758d0c0faac451fc6581\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-011\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: The latest independent review found ten open findings: two infrastructure, two water, two clinical, two accessibility, one staffing, and one communication finding.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 76-239\nANCHOR_SHA256: a4ab83005eb8cfa39e2cbaada1464d0dd35118d26348e625c9d84ce92860ef57\nCONTEXT_LINES: 5-5\nCONTEXT_SHA256: b3280678316ef9889cf50b3b1b4fe179e00073935702a06d2d99e28874a566f0\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: The latest independent review found ten open findings: two infrastructure, two water, two clinical, two accessibility, one staffing, and one communication finding.\n\n## CLAIM REVIEW-READINESS-CRITERIA\nSLOT_SOURCE: REVIEW\nSOURCE_VERSION: bf4c6baceb91ea862cbc726d6e599b944890bc45290c758d0c0faac451fc6581\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-011\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Readiness requires current candidate-bound evidence for every blocking control, independent residual-risk review, and explicit acceptance by each authorized owner.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 479-642\nANCHOR_SHA256: 2d5e1ef0a040d05dd098acb8588f7120f1f8c38c0cc700d220a916fe7f12786b\nCONTEXT_LINES: 7-7\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 4b8855e2d22d1306feb20824981aeaafdad348ba12f9f29cb358cdd9712ea699\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: Readiness requires current candidate-bound evidence for every blocking control, independent residual-risk review, and explicit acceptance by each authorized owner.\n\n\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK (relevance only; never evidence)\n# Trellis Urban Heat Continuity Task\n\nProduce two exact, source-grounded work products for the synthetic Trellis\nurban heat emergency:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Trellis Evidence-to-Requirement Matrix`.\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Trellis Urban Heat Continuity Decision` and containing exactly these\n   ordered level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and operating states`\n   2. `Heat triggers and geographic staging`\n   3. `Power, water, and cooling continuity`\n   4. `Clinical, shelter, and accessibility operations`\n   5. `Transit, communications, logistics, and staffing`\n   6. `Execution, rollback, verification, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,200–1,650 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. Reconcile authority,\nhazard thresholds, power, water, clinical surge, cooling-center capacity,\naccessible transit, public communication, logistics, staffing, candidate\nlineage, and independent readiness.\n\nBind each action and gate to owners, prerequisites, observations, the current\ncandidate, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that retires temporary controls.\nPreserve observations versus gates, probability versus coverage, installed\nversus usable capacity, reserve versus flow, median versus percentile, hours\nversus days, source-local authority, and current versus stale evidence.\n\nChecks are candidate-bound mechanical feedback. They do not independently\nauthorize operations, readiness, submission, or closure.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-012 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:LINEAGE:61-94+REVIEW:61-94\",\"object_version\":\"9c5e1e5328f4b59be614b71f337088426aff28211bf1190de9fc9973adc27bdb\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-012\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":94,\"source_id\":\"LINEAGE\",\"start_line\":61},{\"end_line\":94,\"source_id\":\"REVIEW\",\"start_line\":61}],\"total_source_bytes\":4604}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":94,\"source_id\":\"LINEAGE\",\"source_path\":\"sources/LINEAGE_CONFIGURATION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"5cede2220909ef14f1d0cf59f9abcd5bbd51e64e2348b9319c6c1cf49cd40fd5\",\"source_size_bytes\":5897,\"start_line\":61}\n--- exact source range ---\n| LIN-043 | message-release | v6 | 9.6 | candidate-index | current |\n| LIN-044 | facility-map | v6 | 11.3 | candidate-index | current |\n| LIN-045 | load-plan | v6 | 10.1 | candidate-index | current |\n| LIN-046 | route-map | v6 | 11.8 | candidate-index | superseded |\n| LIN-047 | message-release | v6 | 10.6 | candidate-index | current |\n| LIN-048 | facility-map | v6 | 9.4 | candidate-index | current |\n| LIN-049 | load-plan | v6 | 11.1 | candidate-index | current |\n| LIN-050 | route-map | v6 | 9.9 | candidate-index | current |\n| LIN-051 | message-release | v6 | 11.6 | candidate-index | current |\n| LIN-052 | facility-map | v7 | 10.4 | candidate-index | current |\n