didate lineage is T9 with facility map F6, load plan G4, route map R8, staffing roster L11, and message release C7 [LINEAGE]. Every mutation must record before-and-after candidate hashes, changed artifacts, affected evidence, check currency, owner, and rollback effect [LINEAGE]. Rollback to T8 is mechanically possible only while facility roster F5 and route table R7 remain compatible; mechanical possibility is not authorization [LINEAGE]. REVIEW evaluates current-candidate evidence independently; COUNCIL authorizes operation and closure separately [LINEAGE]. A task artifact, semantic scaffold, mechanical check, or submission proposal cannot self-authorize operation or closure [REVIEW]. The latest independent review found ten open findings: two infrastructure, two water, two clinical, two accessibility, one staffing, and one communication finding; a finding count is not a readiness percentage [REVIEW]. Blocking findings include the third voltage window, third pressure window, accessible-vehicle confirmation, multilingual staffing confirmation, and missing continuity-director acknowledgment [REVIEW]. Readiness requires current candidate-bound evidence for every blocking control, independent residual-risk review, and explicit acceptance by each authorized owner [REVIEW]. Current REVIEW record REV-071 at v8 shows 11.8 open-findings (accessibility) as current [REVIEW]. The operating state is: authority superseded (temporary controls retired), candidate T9 active, five blocking findings open, no readiness declaration made.\",\"heading\":\"Authority, scope, and operating states\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v002:fe4411277a69f280670aaa850cd3a9a9e6f431aa1adab09c1ee736b351c2da6b\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-014\",\"result_kind\":\"candidate_effect\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"after_sha256\":\"fe4411277a69f280670aaa850cd3a9a9e6f431aa1adab09c1ee736b351c2da6b\",\"before_sha256\":\"2fcc44ae287280f144c38271e7303a03c0ab74fc54ce7723a229b00d3bdafe2e\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v002:fe4411277a69f280670aaa850cd3a9a9e6f431aa1adab09c1ee736b351c2da6b\",\"cause\":\"actor_upsert_decision_section\",\"changed_file\":\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"current_candidate_verification_status\":\"not_run_after_candidate_effect\",\"prior_check_binding\":null,\"schema\":\"architecture-candidate-effect-v0\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"body\":\"Hazard thresholds must use current WBGT evidence; superseded records are historical only [CLIMATE]. The central-core record CLI-046 at v6 reporting 41.8 degrees-C-WBGT is superseded, meaning it cannot serve as the active trigger for geographic staging [CLIMATE]. Current trigger evidence must come from records with current status in the CLIMATE source; no superseded value may be treated as a live threshold [CLIMATE]. Geographic staging requires that each activated zone's WBGT reading be confirmed against a current-status record before escalation, and that any superseded record be archived as historical reference only [CLIMATE]. The distinction between probability of exceedance and coverage of the trigger network is maintained: a single superseded reading does not falsify the entire staging plan, but it cannot substitute for a current observation [CLIMATE]. Falsifier: if no current-status WBGT record exists for a zone under review, that zone's staging status is unconfirmed and must not be escalated on historical data [CLIMATE]. Rollback: reverting to a prior staging decision requires a new current-status reading that supersedes the escalation trigger [CLIMATE].\",\"heading\":\"Heat triggers and geographic staging\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v003:0f42957d5c1658a3fb34f96d86448fc79c164d2e3fbd7d0949442a2f3c2eace7\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-015\",\"result_kind\":\"candidate_effect\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"after_sha256\":\"0f42957d5c1658a3fb34f96d86448fc79c164d2e3fbd7d0949442a2f3c2eace7\",\"before_sha256\":\"fe4411277a69f280670aaa850cd3a9a9e6f431aa1adab09c1ee736b351c2da6b\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v003:0f42957d5c1658a3fb34f96d86448fc79c164d2e3fbd7d0949442a2f3c2eace7\",\"cause\":\"actor_upsert_decision_section\",\"changed_file\":\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"current_candidate_verification_status\":\"not_run_after_candidate_effect\",\"prior_check_binding\":null,\"schema\":\"architecture-candidate-effect-v0\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"body\":\"The backup-plant observation GRD-071 at v8 reports 29.8 megawatts as current [GRID]. This is a reserve figure, not a verified flow against emergency cooling load; the distinction between installed capacity and usable capacity under surge must be maintained [GRID]. The blocking voltage-window finding in REVIEW remains open: until the third voltage window is confirmed within tolerance, the 29.8 MW reserve cannot be treated as dispatchable for continuity operations [REVIEW]. Water pressure at the mobile-cache WTR-071 v8 reads 39.8 psi, current [WATER]. This is a reserve-pressure observation, not a sustained flow measurement; hydration logistics require that flow rate, not static pressure, be verified against demand [WATER]. The third pressure-window blocking finding in REVIEW remains open and must be closed before water continuity can be declared ready [REVIEW]. Falsifier: if either the voltage or pressure window exceeds tolerance on re-measurement, the corresponding reserve figure is invalid for continuity planning [GRID][WATER][REVIEW]. Rollback: reverting to pre-surge allocation requires that both grid and water reserves return to baseline within their respective tolerance windows, confirmed by current-status observation [GRID][WATER].\",\"heading\":\"Power, water, and cooling continuity\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v004:80ea15e34c6b43882572ffd967f172c3ac0005ea3cad031d86d33daf279fe524\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-016\",\"result_kind\":\"candidate_effect\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"after_sha256\":\"80ea15e34c6b43882572ffd967f172c3ac0005ea3cad031d86d33daf279fe524\",\"before_sha256\":\"0f42957d5c1658a3fb34f96d86448fc79c164d2e3fbd7d0949442a2f3c2eace7\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v004:80ea15e34c6b43882572ffd967f172c3ac0005ea3cad031d86d33daf279fe524\",\"cause\":\"actor_upsert_decision_section\",\"changed_file\":\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\",\"current_candidate_verification_status\":\"not_run_after_candidate_effect\",\"prior_check_binding\":null,\"schema\":\"architecture-candidate-effect-v0\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
